From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Add an optional Facebook Messenger protocol (prpl-gometa)

Facebook Messenger, end-to-end encrypted chats included, as a second
protocol of the same shared object: a process can host only one Go
c-archive, so a Go-based Facebook plug-in of its own could not be loaded
next to the WhatsApp one. Plain chats go through mautrix-meta's messagix,
encrypted chats through whatsmeow's Facebook client.

It is built only with -DGOMETA=ON, which adds -tags gometa to the Go
build and glue/gometa_init.c and gometabridge.c to the plug-in. Every
Go file of it carries //go:build gometa; with the option off nothing of
it is compiled. It has a C bridge of its own and does not use the
WhatsApp protocol's message path, so the only changes to existing code
are the build option and one call from plugin_init().

Incoming messages are shown as the WhatsApp protocol shows them
(escaped text, quotes, [EDIT], deletions, reactions, locations,
contacts, pictures inline and files as links). docs/FACEBOOK.md
describes building, set-up and the limits.

go.mod gains go.mau.fi/mautrix-meta and, as mautrix-meta's own go.mod,
a replace of github.com/imroc/req/v3 by beeper's fork; version selection
raises github.com/lib/pq and github.com/mattn/go-colorable by a minor
version.

In LuneOS go.mod pins mautrix-meta to its main branch (3f0bb572f0f2,
2026-11-26) instead of a release: Facebook's two-factor code pages now
call a callback maker that v0.2611.0 and earlier do not implement, so
every code submission failed with "unimplemented function dyw (2 args)".
mautrix/meta#633 handles it and is in no release yet. Version selection
moves mautrix-go to v0.33.1-0.20261125114131-b1b4ee3b87d9, whose login
steps carry l10n.Message instructions and LoginInputOption options;
gometa.go reads their text and values. The req replace follows the
revision mautrix-meta's go.mod pins.

